Yet another stupid idea:

Cheshire the neutral extinctionist wizard and general maximizing
munchking, has been at his base level for several months (real time)
sacrificing things, and finally got tired of losing his hard earned
protection every time he accidentally sacrificed a human.

"Fine!," Cheshire thought, "I've got the Eye, and if Thoth is going to
be so picky, he can shove it."  Cheshire went out, bopped a grey
unicorn once or twice with the Staff of Aesculapius, stuck it in his
icebox, took off and dropped the Eyes of the Overworld a few times to
polymorph back from a storm giant to a human, summoned monsters until
he got a nurse, and sacrificed her.  Moments later, Cheshire had the
chilled unicorn ready for sacrifice, and moments after that, Cheshire
was happily chaotic.
 
Except . . .

Now the Staff and Eye are sitting happily in Cheshire's icebox,
worthless, (unless something goes wrong and someone finds an
exceptionally good Lev. 13 bones level), and Cheshire's wasted umpteen
skill levels becoming expert in quarterstaff.  Whoops.  I'll miss the
hungerless regeneration most of all.
 
I'm trying to decide what the abusive munchkin thing to do is in this
case.  I think the most likely solution is for Cheshire to drop
his/her level until s/he loses all of the quarterstaff training, then
level back up, then use a HOA to go lawful for however long it takes
to get Grayswandir.  Thoughts?

